course: dictionary
lesson: 401
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word appear is one of them. The words around it tell you which meaning the writer wants, so always read the whole sentence before you decide.
explain: Appear first means to come into sight, or to begin to be seen. «A rainbow appeared in the sky after the rain.» Nobody was waiting for it. It just came into view.
explain: Appear can also mean to seem. «She appears tired» does not say she is tired for certain. It says she looks tired to us. Try the meaning in the sentence: does «she seems tired» still make sense? Then it is the right one.
explain: Appear can mean to be shown in a film, show, book or list. «The actor appears in the play» means he is one of the people in it. Appear also means to arrive or come into being, as in «new leaves appear in spring».
fact: Appear is a verb, so it changes its form: appear, appears, appeared, appearing.
fact: «Appear» means to come into sight or begin to be seen, as in «a rainbow appeared».
fact: «Appear» can also mean to seem, as in «she appears tired».
fact: «It appears that» means it seems that something is true, based on what we can see or know.
fact: A word with more than one meaning is called a multi-meaning word. Use the context to choose the right meaning.
exercise: «A rainbow appeared after the rain.» What does appeared mean here? | *Came into sight | Was painted on the sky by hand | Fell down | Went away for ever
exercise: «She appears tired.» What does appears mean in this sentence? | Is tired for certain | Runs very fast | *Seems tired | Is asleep
exercise: Mia reads «the actor appears in the play». What does appears mean here? | To sing very loudly | To disappear | *To be one of the people shown in a play | To fall over on the stage
test: «New leaves appear in spring.» What does appear mean here? | To be painted green | *To arrive or come into being | To stop growing | To fall off the tree
test: «It appears that the bread has mould on it.» What does appears mean here? | It is cut into slices | It disappears from the kitchen | It is certainly true for ever | *It seems, from what we can see
exam: «Suddenly, a ghost appeared at the window.» What does appeared mean? | Went out of the room | Cleaned the window | *Came into sight, suddenly | Ate some bread
